* START-HISTORY:
* 20 Sep 26 dm THE BATCH GATE (S.40), PARITY WITH THE WINDOWS PORT.  Owner's
*           ruling, 20 Sep 2026: a behavior prevented on one port must be
*           prevented on both, the mechanism free to differ with the OS.  A
*           single-command invocation ("sd '<command>'", system(1026)) is now
*           admitted by an ELEVATED session as before, or by the account's own
*           list in SDSYS batch.jobs (one command, no arguments, VOC type PA
*           or S), refused otherwise (11000-11002).  See batch.permitted.
*           Before this, CPROC ran any command line unconditionally once the
*           account was entered - Linux never had either half of what Windows
*           built 22 Aug 2026 (its batch.jobs, PROJECT_STATUS.md 7 step 9).
* 18 Sep 26 dm TEARDOWN (owner's 18 Sep 2026 decision).  The tier machinery is
*           out: update.voc copies all of NEWVOC with no STANDARD omit filter
*           and no administrator add layer (one VOC layer, S.25); get.acc.tier
*           and the tier resolution in the UPDATE.ACCOUNTS ALL walk are gone.
*           The suspended test reads ACC$SUSPENDED (W.7) and the OS-access
*           grant load is gone - SH and OS.EXECUTE run at the account's own
*           Linux permissions (S.27).
* 14 Sep 26 dm  The $release prompt (5026) takes N on Enter and at end of
*               input, and says so (PROJECT_STATUS S.9).
* 13 Sep 26 dm  Tier omit/add lists read from sdsys/tier.policy, not NEWVOC
*               (plan M / port a47526f): opened fail-safe, skip tests gone.
* 13 Sep 26 dm  No longer turns case inversion on at sign-on (plan M).
* 13 Sep 26 dm  Account names are lower case, SDSYS included (plan M, owner's
*               rulings of 12 and 13 Sep): the register key is the lower-cased
*               name, so every name taken from input, @LOGNAME or a path is
*               downcased before the lookup, and @WHO reads 'sdsys', 'don'.
* 13 Sep 26 dm  Reads the $release and $command.stack VOC records by their
*               lower-case ids (plan M3, the $ records).  Exact reads, and
*               there are no accounts from before the rename (owner).
* 13 Sep 26 dm  An account's VOC file is voc on disk (plan M3 D3).
* 13 Sep 26 dm  Opens sdsys accounts, $ipc, newvoc and voc_template by their
*               lower-case names on disk (plan M3 D1).
* 12 Sep 26 dm  The case migration added to update.voc earlier today is
*               removed: there are no existing installs to migrate (owner).
* 11 Sep 26 dm  update.voc now also adds the ADMINISTRATOR tier layer from
*               VOC_TEMPLATE, which it never read before, so an upgrade brings
*               an existing administrator the verbs added since its account was
*               made (PORT_ADOPTION 16; measured gap: DON was missing 8 of 18).
*               Adds only what is absent, never overwrites, never removes, and
*               only for an explicit ADMINISTRATOR tier.  Message 10912.
* 11 Sep 26 dm  Every sign-on and every refused sign-on, with its reason, is
*               written to the audit trail (PORT_ADOPTION 13, the port's).
* 11 Sep 26 dm  A suspended account is refused at sign-on, console and ssh
*               alike (10107; PORT_ADOPTION 12, the port's LOGIN).
* 11 Sep 26 dm  A TERM with no shipped terminfo entry falls back to linux
*               instead of leaving the login with no capabilities (UPSTREAM
*               12, as the port).  update.voc leaves a record marked
*               [locked] alone, except a verb, and names both kinds (10165,
*               10166; port PRE_RELEASE_FIXES 70).
* 10 Sep 26 dm  Parity audit: mode 4 is UPDATE.ACCOUNTS ALL (port PRE_RELEASE_FIXES
*               70), and update.voc writes records whole (port 136).
* 10 Sep 26 dm  SL1 - update.voc applies the account's tier, so a VOC update
*               (the $RELEASE prompt, UPDATE.ACCOUNTS, or the all-accounts walk)
*               no longer hands a STANDARD account back the verbs CREATEA left
*               out.  The port's 17 Aug 2026 fix.  old.rec is also cleared
*               before each READU (the port's fix of the same day).
* rev 0.9.1 Mar 25 mab return to single rev tracking
* rev 0.9.0 Jan 25 mab change permission required for account login, must now either be;
*                      1) users ACCOUNT
*                      2) member of the ACCOUNT's linux group
*                      regardles must be a member of sdusers
*                      3) if user started with sudo sd, cproc should have set K$ADMINISTRATOR
*                         and dropped user to sdsys. we no longer test system(27) (uid of process)
*
* 20240612 dsm removed read/write $LOGINS
* 20240330 mab rev 064 mods to $LOGINS / ACCOUNTS
* 19 Jan 04  0.6.1 SD launch. Earlier history details suppressed.
* END-HISTORYPTION:
*
* Mode argument:
*   0   Interactive user
*   1   SDApiSrvr session
*   2   Updating VOC only
*   3   End of install - offer to upgrade all VOCs (non-GPL version only)
*   4   UPDATE.ACCOUNTS ALL - this VOC, then every registered account, unasked
*
